4. Findings Across Operational Sections

Application Disk Requirements: The existing 19-day snapshot gap exposed Bright Path to catastrophic data loss, failing their 24-hour RPO. Automated Amazon Data Lifecycle Manager (DLM) policies paired with gp3 volumes resolve this gap.

Shared Working Files: Traditional block storage cannot handle concurrent multi-server access. Amazon EFS provides the necessary POSIX-compliant, multi-instance read/write file sharing.

Document Ingestion: Amazon S3 Standard offers scalable object storage with robust HTTP REST API access for incoming documents.

Archival Retention: Storing records in Amazon S3 Glacier combined with S3 Object Lock (Compliance Mode) fulfills the strict 7-year immutable retention mandate without risk of premature deletion.

Recovery Verification: Automated snapshots and lifecycle rules must be audited regularly via CLI inspection (describe-snapshots, head-object) to ensure compliance.

Access Patterns & Cost Optimization: Transitioning inactive files to EFS Infrequent Access (IA) and S3 Glacier reduces long-term storage expenditures.

Resource Hygiene: Purging temporary test artifacts prevents resource drift, accidental cost accumulation, and dormant security vulnerabilities.

5. Storage Recommendation Matrix

Data Category	Recommended Storage Model	Primary Access Pattern	Recovery & Retention Strategy
Application Disk	Amazon EBS (Block)	Low-latency, direct block access	Daily automated EBS snapshots via AWS DLM (24-hr RPO)
Shared Working Files	Amazon EFS (File)	Concurrent POSIX-compliant file access across multiple hosts	Continuous multi-AZ replication & automated lifecycle tiering
Uploaded Documents	Amazon S3 Standard (Object)	Direct REST API calls (GET, PUT) via flat namespace	Versioning enabled to protect against accidental overwrites
Seven-Year Records	Amazon S3 Glacier (Object)	Infrequent/archival access with regulatory audit requirements	S3 Object Lock (Compliance Mode) for a strict 7-year retention period
6. Recovery and Retention Verification

RPO Compliance: Automated DLM schedules must be verified daily to ensure snapshots complete within the 24-hour window.

Immutable Compliance Lock: S3 Object Lock in Compliance Mode prevents even root administrators from shortening or deleting retention periods, safeguarding records against tampering. Legal and compliance sign-off is mandatory before deployment.

